{"abstract":"In this paper we introduce and describe the phenomenon of videogame street art as a specific kind of street art. We consider its materiality and significance, and conceptualize it in the light of a double manifestation of play: the playful appropriation of the city by the artist and the fact that street art encapsulates the act of playing videogames in a visual form. Digital play spills out of our computer screens and occupies the urban space with the explicit intention of involving spectators, who are invited to play in symbolic ways that actualize nostalgic memories of gaming and can be related to a more general \"play turn\" in our culture.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Vazques Marquez, Israel","Pajares Tosca, Susana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384311"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["City","Graffiti","Play","Street art","Videogames"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"playing with the city street art and videogames","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5209/ARIS.51892","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384311","identifier":[{"id":"85015153675","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cfaadc6c-5b2b-44bd-901a-d3e433dede4f"],"keyword":["Street art","city","graffiti","play","videogames"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2477B239918DD3E718A7BA82A3AD6A42"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81876595/51892_107117_2_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5209/ARIS.51892","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Digital Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Israel","key":"vazquesmarquezpau","last":"Vazques Marquez","locid":"1dfe5d85-a1cc-4810-b5f7-7790e77896b9","name":"Vazques Marquez, Israel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susana","key":"pajarestoscapau","last":"Pajares Tosca","name":"Pajares Tosca, Susana","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5209/aris.51892","issn":["11315598","16959477"],"issn_org":["11315598"],"issue":"1","journal":"Arte, Individuo y Sociedad","pages":"105-120","publisher":"Universidad Complutense de Madrid","status":"p","title":"Arte, Individuo y Sociedad","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015153675"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cfaadc6c-5b2b-44bd-901a-d3e433dede4f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Playing With the City: Street Art and Videogames","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384311","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
